## ⚡ Section 3: Class-D Amplifiers & Safe Power Supplies

Desktop Class-D amplifiers switch DC supply rails directly into the speaker load via an LC reconstruction filter—meaning **power supply quality directly determines bass punch, noise floor, and hardware safety**.

### 3.1 Stereo Amplifier Selection & Safe Voltage Matching

* **Compact Stereo Class-D Tier (`TI TPA3116`, ~£20–£45):** **Nobsound NS-20G** (dual TPA3116, 30-step digital encoder + front 3.5 mm `AUX` jack), **Nobsound NS-01G Pro**, or **Douk Audio / Sabaj TPA3116** 2-channel stereo amps. *(Ensure you pick a 2-channel stereo amp, not a mono subwoofer amp like the Douk NS-03G.)*
  * **Safe PSU:** Rated 12V–24V DC (`5.5 × 2.5 mm` centre-positive). Use a regulated **19V/4.74A (90W)** or **20V/4.5A (90W)** brick (e.g., genuine Dell/Lenovo/HP laptop brick with adapter, or Mean Well `GST90A19`), or a regulated `24V/4A–5A` supply—staying safely below the TPA3116's 26V ceiling and 25V smoothing capacitors.
* **Amp-Free Active Alternative:** If you prefer zero external amplifier or power brick, pair your USB-C DAC directly with **Wharfedale Pro Diamond Studio (5-BT / 7-BT)** bi-amped monitors (`2.0 Vrms` line-out straight into balanced TRS/XLR or RCA inputs).

### 3.2 Power Supply Buying Rules

| Category | Recommended Power Supplies (Buy) | Hazardous Power Supplies (Avoid) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Brand & Topology** | **Mean Well** industrial units (`GST90A19` / `GST160A24`), or **genuine Dell/Lenovo/HP 19V–20V laptop bricks**. | Unbranded generic `24V/48V` bricks from online marketplaces, adjustable multi-voltage rotary wall warts, or cheap `12V/2A` router adapters. |
| **Electrical Safety & Noise** | Proper UKCA/CE isolation, low switching ripple (`< 100 mV p-p`), genuine over-current/short-circuit protection, and tight barrel contacts. | Fake current ratings (voltage sags on bass transients), missing EMI filters (injects high-pitched whine into speakers), and poor mains isolation. |
| **Voltage Discipline** | Stay at least `2V–4V` below internal smoothing capacitor ratings (`25V` caps on standard TPA3116 boards). | Feeding `24V+` into a TPA3116 board with `25V` capacitors—causes capacitor venting/failure. |

